# AROS Git Repository [![Codacy Badge](https://app.codacy.com/project/badge/Grade/8dd5a86f87064c14ba75f291c045e788)](https://app.codacy.com/gh/aros-development-team/AROS/dashboard)

> This is the main repository for active development of the AROS Operating System.
> The repository contains the main Operating System components, SDK and Build System.

## 📚 Documentation

**→ All project documentation is located in the [`docs/`](docs/) directory.**

- **For AI Agents & Developers:** Start with [`DOCUMENTATION_GUIDE.md`](DOCUMENTATION_GUIDE.md)
- **Workflow Guide:** [`docs/AGENTIC_AI_WORKFLOW.md`](docs/AGENTIC_AI_WORKFLOW.md)
- **Documentation Index:** [`docs/README.md`](docs/README.md)

The documentation follows a per-project structure to keep everything organized and accessible.

## 🤖 Dual-Agent Autonomous Build System (NEW!)

AROS now includes a revolutionary **dual-agent autonomous build system** that uses two specialized LLM agents working together through an **ACD (Autonomous Continuous Development) exchange of thought** protocol:

- **🎨 Generator Agent** (`richardyoung/uigen-x-30b-moe`) - Creates code solutions and fixes
- **🧠 Reasoning Agent** (`huihui_ai/gpt-oss-abliterated`) - Analyzes, validates, and provides feedback

### Key Features
- ✨ **Collaborative AI**: Two agents work together for better solutions
- 🔄 **ACD Exchange Protocol**: Structured generate → reason → refine → validate workflow
- 🚦 **Communication Flags**: Rich signaling (CONFIDENT/UNCERTAIN, REQUEST_FEEDBACK, READY/DONE)
- 🎮 **Dual-GPU Support**: Parallel execution on separate GPUs
- 🛠️ **Build Error Resolution**: Automatic fix generation with validation

### Quick Start

```bash
# Install models
ollama pull richardyoung/uigen-x-30b-moe:q6_k
ollama pull huihui_ai/gpt-oss-abliterated

# Run example
python3 scripts/dual_agent_example.py

# Use for your own problems
python3 scripts/dual_agent_orchestrator.py \
    --problem "Fix undeclared identifier error" \
    --output results.json
```

📖 **Learn More**: 
- [Quick Start Guide](DUAL_AGENT_QUICKSTART.md) - Get started in 5 minutes
- [Full Documentation](DUAL_AGENT_SYSTEM.md) - Complete guide
- [ACD Standard v1.0](ACD_SPECIFICATION_V1.md) - Complete specification with AROS extensions
- [Official ACD Standard](https://github.com/RECALLInstituteACD/Autonomous-Continuous-Development-ACD-Standard-Specification) - RECALL Institute specification


## Nightly Test Builds


* Builds are scheduled to run starting at 00:00 UTC. LLVM builds generally start 2hrs later.
* The builds are made using the scripts/azure-pipelines.yml file. Further details can be found in that file.
* GCC 6.5.0 builds are configured using default toolchain settings. Newer GCC builds may also use newer versions of binutils.
* The main AROS target and distfiles are built for each arch.
* The builds are downloadable via http://www.aros.org/nightly1.html [![Download AROS Research Operating System](https://img.shields.io/sourceforge/dt/aros.svg)](http://www.aros.org/nightly1.html).

