## Getting Started

### Cloning the Repository

To clone the AROS repository with all submodules:

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/terminills/AROS-OLD.git
cd AROS-OLD

# Option 1: Use the interactive setup script (recommended)
./setup-submodules.sh

# Option 2: Initialize all submodules manually
git submodule update --init --recursive
```

### Essential Submodules

This repository includes several important submodules:

**Core AROS Components:**
- **contrib** - Contributed applications, games, and utilities
- **ports** - Ported software packages (audio, graphics, development tools, etc.)
- **documentation** - Multilingual AROS documentation

**Emulation:**
- **emumiga** (`external/emumiga/`) - MC68K (68000) CPU emulation layer for running legacy Amiga applications without UAE

**Build Tools:**
- **depot_tools** (`external/electron/v8/depot_tools/`) - Chromium build tools required for V8 JavaScript engine

**Translation Catalogs:**
- Multiple translation submodules for internationalization support

### Initializing Specific Submodules

If you only need specific components:

```bash
# For contributed applications and games
git submodule update --init contrib

# For ported software packages
git submodule update --init ports

# For AROS documentation
git submodule update --init documentation

# For MC68K emulation (running legacy 68k Amiga apps)
git submodule update --init external/emumiga

# For V8 build tools (if working on JavaScript engine)
git submodule update --init external/electron/v8/depot_tools

# For translation catalogs
git submodule update --init --recursive workbench/libs/muimaster/catalogs
```

## Building AROS

For comprehensive build instructions, including how to build AROS for PC x86_64 with SMP support using the latest cross-compilers, please see:

📖 **[BUILDING.md](BUILDING.md) - Complete Build Guide**

The build guide covers:
- Prerequisites and system requirements
- Configuring AROS with different toolchains (GCC/LLVM)
- Building for PC x86_64 with SMP (Symmetric Multi-Processing)
- Understanding and parsing compiler error messages
- Troubleshooting common build issues
- Advanced configuration options

### Quick Start

For a basic PC x86_64 SMP build:

```bash
# Install dependencies (Ubuntu/Debian)
sudo apt-get install -y build-essential gawk bison flex netpbm automake cmake \
    libpng-dev zlib1g-dev libxcursor-dev libgl1-mesa-dev libasound2-dev \
    python3-mako libswitch-perl gperf gcc-multilib g++ ccache genisoimage \
    jlha-utils wget liblzma-dev mtools xorriso nasm

# Configure for pc-x86_64 with SMP (using GCC 15.2.0 required for V8)
./configure --target=pc-x86_64 --enable-target-variant=smp --with-gcc-version=15.2.0 --enable-ccache

# Build cross-compiler toolchain (first time only)
make -j$(nproc) crosstools

# Build AROS
make -j$(nproc)
```

### Automated Builds with GitHub Actions

**🤖 NEW: Automated AROS Builds**

We provide a GitHub Actions workflow to build AROS with GCC 15+ automatically:

**Benefits:**
- ✅ No local setup required
- ✅ Build AROS in the cloud
- ✅ Pre-built cross-compiler toolchains (saves 1-2 hours)
- ✅ Bootable ISO images
- ✅ Supports V8/Node.js/Electron development (GCC 15+ with C++20)

**How to use:**
1. Go to [Actions tab](../../actions)
2. Select "Build AROS with GCC 15+"
3. Click "Run workflow"
4. Download build artifacts (toolchain + ISO)

📖 **Learn More:** See [.github/workflows/BUILD_AROS_WORKFLOW_GUIDE.md](.github/workflows/BUILD_AROS_WORKFLOW_GUIDE.md)

## Incorporated components

AROS contains a number of projects that have been donated to the codebase, you can find links to them here.


* [![AHI](https://github.com/aros-development-team/AROS/blob/master/images/Logos/AHI.png?raw=true)](../master/workbench/devs/AHI/README.md) - The de-facto standard retargetable audio system for AROS, AmigaOS, and MorphOS.

* [Poseidon](../master/rom/usb/README.md) - Modular USB host stack for Amiga-like systems.



## Syncing with Upstream

This repository is a fork of the official [aros-development-team/AROS](https://github.com/aros-development-team/AROS) repository. To get the latest compilers, toolchain patches, and improvements:

```bash
./scripts/sync-upstream.sh
```

See [SYNC_UPSTREAM.md](SYNC_UPSTREAM.md) for detailed instructions.

